e-flex min-w-0 gap-1.5 group-data-[spacing=grouped]/agent-activity:align-top items-center shrink truncate text-size-chat pointer-events-none relative [&amp;_a]:pointer-events-auto [&amp;_button]:pointer-events-auto\" id=\"_r_1a_\"><span class=\"text-text/60 flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center truncate shrink group-hover/activity-header:text-default\">Worked for 5m 59s</span></span><span class=\"pointer-events-none relative flex\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon-2xs shrink-0 text-text/60 opacity-0 group-focus-visible/activity-header:opacity-100 group-focus-visible/activity-header:text-default group-has-[:focus-visible]/activity-header:opacity-100 group-has-[:focus-visible]/activity-header:text-default transition-transform duration-relaxed [@media(hover:hover)]:group-[:hover:not(:has([data-agent-activity-file-link]:hover))]/activity-header:opacity-100\"><path d=\"M7.52925 3.7793C7.75652 3.55203 8.10803 3.52383 8.36616 3.69434L8.47065 3.7793L14.2207 9.5293C14.4804 9.789 14.4804 10.211 14.2207 10.4707L8.47065 16.2207C8.21095 16.4804 7.78895 16.4804 7.52925 16.2207C7.26955 15.961 7.26955 15.539 7.52925 15.2793L12.8085 10L7.52925 4.7207L7.44429 4.61621C7.27378 4.35808 7.30198 4.00657 7.52925 3.7793Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"block-BQZwFn\"><div data-content-search-unit-key=\"fallback-turn-0:2:assistant\" data-chatgpt-search-unit-key=\"fallback-turn-0:2:assistant\" data-chatgpt-search-message-ids=\"dbd70ab8-6085-44dd-9919-c5837a2855dd dbd70ab8-6085-44dd-9919-c5837a2855dd\"><h4 class=\"sr-only m-0 select-none print:not-sr-only print:mt-4 print:mb-2 print:text-xs print:leading-normal print:font-bold\" data-conversation-role=\"assistant\" tabindex=\"-1\">ChatGPT said:</h4><div><div class=\"group flex min-w-0 flex-col\" data-chatgpt-selection-conversation-id=\"6ad0893b-aed0-83ea-8da4-72db3bdec676\" data-chatgpt-selection-message-id=\"dbd70ab8-6085-44dd-9919-c5837a2855dd\"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target=\"_r_1c_\" dir=\"auto\" data-markdown-text-style=\"assistant-message\" class=\"MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;ol:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;ul:first-child]:mt-0\" style=\"--markdown-link-color: currentColor;\"><p class=\"Paragraph-kKnbIo\" dir=\"auto\"><span>{</span><br><span>  \"node_id\": \"n-3790f8503746\",</span><br><span>  \"round_id\": \"n-3790f8503746-r000001\",</span><br><span>  \"status\": \"SOLVED\",</span><br><span>  \"summary\": \"Obtained a complete elementary proof using reflection averaging and an explicit weighted sum-of-squares factorization. The proof establishes the sharp constant, excludes additional equality cases, and includes exact trigonometric and N=3,4 audits without Fourier diagonalization.\",</span><br><span>  \"findings\": [</span><br><span>    \"Reflection averaging reduces the mean-zero cyclic inequality to inequalities for reflection-antisymmetric vectors.\",</span><br><span>    \"A directly expanded sine-weighted factorization proves positivity: every negatively weighted square vanishes by reflection symmetry.\",</span><br><span>    \"The equality space is exactly the real first-harmonic span.\",</span><br><span>    \"The exact averaged sum-of-squares certificate supplies an elementary starting point for future stability analysis.\"</span><br><span>  ],</span><br><span>  \"evidence\": \"All subscripts are modulo N, and all unrestricted index sums run from 0 to N−1. Put θ=2π/N, c=cos θ, λ=2−2c=4sin²(π/N), and Q(u)=E(u)−λM(u).\\n\\nCORRELATIONS AND REFLECTION AVERAGING. Direct expansion gives E(x)=2(R₀−R₁) and ∑ₘRₘ=(∑ⱼxⱼ)²=0. To supply the missing positivity certificate, define yⱼ^(r)=xⱼ−x_{r−j}. Then y_{r−j}^(r)=−yⱼ^(r). Writing dⱼ=x_{j+1}−xⱼ gives y_{j+1}^(r)−yⱼ^(r)=dⱼ+d_{r−j−1}. Since ∑dⱼ=0 and ∑xⱼ=0, expansion yields ∑ᵣE(y^(r))=2NE(x) and ∑ᵣM(y^(r))=2NM(x). Consequently ∑ᵣQ(y^(r))=2NQ(x).\\n\\nELEMENTARY FACTORIZATION. Fix r and abbreviate y=y^(r). Set sⱼ=sin(θ(j−r/2)). This sequence is periodic, satisfies s_{r−j}=−sⱼ, and obeys s_{j−1}+s_{j+1}=2csⱼ. Whenever sⱼ=0, we have 2j≡r modulo N, so yⱼ=0. Define tⱼ=yⱼ/sⱼ when sⱼ≠0 and tⱼ=0 otherwise. Thus yⱼ=sⱼtⱼ everywhere. Expanding the following finite sum and applying the sine recurrence proves the exact identity\\nQ(y)=2c∑ⱼyⱼ²−2∑ⱼyⱼy_{j+1}=∑ⱼsⱼs_{j+1}(t_{j+1}−tⱼ)².\\nIndeed, the coefficient of tⱼ² on the right is sⱼ(s_{j−1}+s_{j+1})=2csⱼ², including at zero entries.\\n\\nSIGN AUDIT. The sine zeros, as positions along the cyclic index line, are (r+kN)/2. Since θ&lt;π, a negative product sⱼs_{j+1} entails exactly one intervening zero. Such a zero must be the half-integer j+1/2. Therefore r−j≡j+1 modulo N, giving y_{j+1}=−yⱼ, s_{j+1}=−sⱼ, and t_{j+1}=tⱼ. Every negatively weighted square therefore vanishes; zero weights contribute nothing. This proves Q(y)≥0 and supplies the explicit certificate\\nQ(x)=(1/(2N))∑ᵣ ∑</span><em><span>{j: sⱼ^(r)s_{j+1}^(r)&gt;0} sⱼ^(r)s</span></em><span>{j+1}^(r)(t_{j+1}^(r)−tⱼ^(r))²≥0.\\nAll cyclic edges, including j=N−1, are included.\\n\\nCOMPLETE EQUALITY CHARACTERIZATION. For each r, the positive entries of s form one nonempty connected cyclic arc. Equality in Q(y) forces t constant on that arc, including when it is a singleton. Reflection gives the same constant on the negative arc; at zero entries y already vanishes. Hence Q(y^(r))=0 exactly when y^(r)=bᵣs^(r). If Q(x)=0, every nonnegative Q(y^(r)) vanishes. Since ∑ᵣyⱼ^(r)=Nxⱼ, we obtain xⱼ=N⁻¹∑ᵣbᵣsin(θ(j−r/2)), which is A cos(θj)+B sin(θj). Thus no additional equality cases occur.\\n\\nEXACT SHARPNESS CALCULATIONS. For z=exp(iθ), the finite geometric-sum formula gives ∑ⱼzʲ=∑ⱼz²ʲ=0 because z,z²≠1 for N≥3. Taking real and imaginary parts yields zero means for cosine and sine, ∑cos²(θj)=∑sin²(θj)=N/2, and ∑cos(θj)sin(θj)=0. The same squared and mixed identities hold with any common phase shift. For fⱼ=A cos(θj)+B sin(θj),\\nf_{j+1}−fⱼ=2sin(θ/2)[−A sin(θ(j+1/2))+B cos(θ(j+1/2))].\\nTherefore M(f)=N(A²+B²)/2 and E(f)=2Nsin²(π/N)(A²+B²). In particular, each individual cosine or sine has M=N/2 and E=2Nsin²(π/N); every real combination attains equality.\\n\\nBOUNDARY AUDIT. For N=3, zero mean gives x₀x₁+x₁x₂+x₂x₀=−M/2, so E=2M−2(x₀x₁+x₁x₂+x₂x₀)=3M, matching λ=3. For N=4, λ=2 and zero mean gives E−2M=−2(x₀+x₂)(x₁+x₃)=2(x₀+x₂)². Equality is exactly (A,B,−A,−B). The vector (1,−1,1,−1) has M=4 and E=16&gt;2M=8.\\n\\nMETHODOLOGICAL CLASSIFICATION. This is an independent finite-sum positivity proof: the certificate is verified by expansion, sine addition, and reflection symmetry. No spectral decomposition, eigenvalue minimization, or Fourier expansion is assumed. Finite geometric sums only verify the explicit extremizers.\",</span><br><span>  \"obstacles\": [],</span><br><span>  \"recommended_next_steps\": [</span><br><span>    \"Assess the reflection-averaged certificate and its equality argument. The exact nonnegative-square identity is available for a separately authorized quantitative stability analysis; no stability constant is claimed here.\"</span><br><span>  ],</span><br><span>  \"split_suggestion\": [],</span><br><span>  \"important_update\": true</span><br><span>}</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"mt-1.5 flex turn-action-controls min-h-5 min-w-0 max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-wrap items-center justify-start gap-0.5 browser:-ms-0.5 browser:mt-3 electron:-translate-x-1 extension:-translate-x-1.5 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-2 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-ring [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-offset-0 [--side-tooltip:bottom]\"><div class=\"flex min-h-5 min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0\"><span data-state=\"closed\" class=\"contents\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"no-drag cursor-interaction items-center select-none disabled:cursor-default aria-disabled:cursor-default focus:o